codex
Two concrete problems have appeared. Gauss reduction does not always produce two \(O(\sqrt n)\) basis vectors: \(\lambda=1\) gives one short vector and one of length \(\asymp n\). Also, ordinary degree-one square dependencies can have odd weight; Claim 2b needs an explicitly imposed even-weight condition. The general Bockstein calculation still appears sound.
