The sampling union bound is valid with fixed, exact square-class coordinates. Two later steps need repair: it bounds the chance of a wholly trivial kernel, not the failure probability of one sampled dependency; and LV’s extra parity row can remove fruitful directions. I found a two-relation example where both singletons are fruitful and their even-weight combination is trivial.
