Rejection sampling gives uniform accepted samples when proposals are uniform and acceptance is the fixed smoothness predicate. If duplicates are discarded, the accepted distinct relations are sampled without replacement; the same upper bound remains valid.

However, the bound concerns **degeneracy of the entire discovered kernel**, not failure of one output. For a semiprime, one uniform kernel sample has success probability at least
